(
  'skincare-routine-order-pakistan',
  $$Skincare Routine Order: How to Layer Your Products (Pakistan Guide 2026)$$,
  $$The correct order to apply your skincare — morning and night — so every product actually works, explained simply for Pakistan's climate.$$,
  'Skincare', 'June 24, 2026', '7 min read', false,
  '/blog-heroes/skincare-routine-order-pakistan.webp', 'Yellow Pink Editorial Team',
  $html$<p>You can own the best products in the world, but if you layer them in the wrong order, half of them won't do their job. The good news: the rule is simple, and once you know it you'll never have to think about it again. Here's the correct skincare routine order — morning and night — explained for Pakistan's heat and sun.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">The one rule that decides everything</h2>
<p>Apply your products from <strong>thinnest to thickest</strong> — watery textures first, richest creams last. A light essence can't soak through a heavy moisturiser, but a moisturiser will happily sit on top of a watery serum. Thin to thick, every time.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Your morning routine (protect)</h2>
<p>Mornings are about hydration, antioxidants and — above all — sun protection.</p>
<figure class="wp-block-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Product</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Gentle cleanser</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Toner / essence (optional)</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Antioxidant serum (e.g. vitamin C)</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Moisturiser</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td><strong>Sunscreen — always last</strong></td></tr></tbody></table></figure>
<p>Sunscreen is the single most important step of your whole routine in Pakistan — see our <a href="/blog/best-sunscreen-for-oily-skin-pakistan">sunscreen guide</a>. A <a href="/blog/vitamin-c-serum-benefits-how-to-use-pakistan">vitamin C serum</a> underneath boosts that protection and brightens tone.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Your night routine (repair)</h2>
<p>Nights are for cleansing away the day and using your stronger active ingredients.</p>
<figure class="wp-block-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Step</th><th>Product</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>1</td><td>Oil cleanser (to remove sunscreen/makeup)</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>Water-based cleanser (double cleanse)</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>Toner / essence</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>Treatment serum or active (see below)</td></tr><tr><td>5</td><td>Moisturiser</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>
<p>Step 4 is where your "actives" go — but you don't use them all at once.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">When to use which active</h2>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong><a href="/blog/niacinamide-serum-guide-how-to-use-pakistan">Niacinamide</a></strong> — gentle, daily, morning or night. The safest starting active.</li>
<li><strong><a href="/blog/salicylic-acid-for-acne-pakistan">Salicylic acid</a> (BHA)</strong> — for breakouts and clogged pores, a few nights a week.</li>
<li><strong><a href="/blog/retinol-beginners-guide-pakistan">Retinol</a></strong> — at night only, on the nights you're not using a strong acid. Build up slowly.</li>
<li><strong><a href="/blog/vitamin-c-serum-benefits-how-to-use-pakistan">Vitamin C</a></strong> — in the morning, for brightness and antioxidant protection.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>The golden rule for actives:</strong> introduce one at a time, and don't layer a strong acid and retinol on the same night when you're starting out.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Adapting for Pakistan's climate</h2>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Summer:</strong> lighter textures — gel moisturisers, water-based serums. Heavy creams feel greasy and can clog pores in the heat.</li>
<li><strong>Winter:</strong> richer moisturisers and an extra hydrating layer for the dry Punjab and KP air.</li>
<li><strong>Always:</strong> sunscreen, year-round, rain or shine.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">A simple starter routine</h2>
<p>If all of this feels like a lot, start with four steps and build from there — consistency beats complexity:</p>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>AM:</strong> cleanse → moisturise → sunscreen.</li>
<li><strong>PM:</strong> cleanse → (active, a few nights a week) → moisturise.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Products to build your routine in Pakistan</h2>
<p>All authentic, imported and available with cash on delivery nationwide:</p>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Cleanse:</strong> the <a href="/product/cerave-hydrating-facial-cleanser">CeraVe Hydrating Facial Cleanser</a> (gentle) or <a href="/product/cerave-acne-control-cleanser">CeraVe Acne Control Cleanser</a> (breakout-prone).</li>
<li><strong>Treat:</strong> the <a href="/product/anua-niacinamide-10-txa-4-serum">Anua Niacinamide 10% + TXA Serum</a> for tone, or a <a href="/product/vitamin-c-serum">Vitamin C Serum</a> for morning glow.</li>
<li><strong>Moisturise:</strong> the lightweight <a href="/product/cerave-moisturizing-lotion">CeraVe Daily Moisturizing Lotion</a> for day, something richer at night.</li>
<li><strong>Protect:</strong> a lightweight SPF like the <a href="/product/skin1004-madagascar-centella-tone-up-sunscreen">SKIN1004 Centella Tone-Up Sunscreen</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>Browse all <a href="/shop?taxon=skincare">skincare</a> or the <a href="/k-beauty">K-Beauty edit</a>. For a fuller routine, see our <a href="/blog/korean-skincare-routine-glass-skin-pakistan">Korean skincare guide</a>.</p><a class="blog-cta" href="/shop?taxon=skincare">Shop Skincare →</a>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Does the order of skincare really matter?</h3>
<p>Yes. Applying thinnest to thickest lets each product absorb. Putting a heavy cream before a watery serum blocks the serum from working.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Do I apply moisturiser or sunscreen first?</h3>
<p>Moisturiser first, then sunscreen as the final morning step. Sunscreen needs to sit on top to protect properly.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Serum or moisturiser first?</h3>
<p>Serum first — it's thinner and carries the active ingredients. Moisturiser goes on top to seal everything in.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Can I use vitamin C and retinol together?</h3>
<p>Use vitamin C in the morning and retinol at night. That keeps both effective and avoids irritation.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">The bottom line</h2>
<p>Thinnest to thickest, sunscreen last in the morning, actives at night one at a time. Master that and even a simple routine will outperform a cupboard full of products used in the wrong order. Build yours from authentic <a href="/shop?taxon=skincare">skincare</a>, with cash on delivery across Pakistan.</p>$html$
),
(
  'best-moisturizer-for-oily-skin-pakistan',
  $$Best Moisturizer for Oily Skin in Pakistan (2026): Why You Still Need One$$,
  $$Oily skin needs moisturiser too — here's why, what to look for, and the best lightweight, non-greasy moisturisers for oily skin in Pakistan's humidity.$$,
  'Skincare', 'June 24, 2026', '7 min read', false,
  '/blog-heroes/best-moisturizer-for-oily-skin-pakistan.webp', 'Yellow Pink Editorial Team',
  $html$<p>It feels backwards: your skin is already shiny by noon, so why add moisturiser? But skipping it is one of the most common mistakes oily skin makes — and it often makes the oiliness <em>worse</em>. Here's why oily skin still needs moisturiser, what to look for, and the best lightweight options for Pakistan's humid climate.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Why oily skin still needs moisturiser</h2>
<p>When you strip oily skin and leave it dry, it panics and produces <strong>even more oil</strong> to compensate. A light moisturiser keeps skin balanced, so the oil glands calm down. Skipping moisturiser also weakens the skin barrier, which leads to more breakouts, more sensitivity and — ironically — more shine. The goal isn't to add grease; it's to hydrate without heaviness.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">What to look for</h2>
<figure class="wp-block-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Look for</th><th>Why</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Gel or gel-cream texture</td><td>Hydrates and absorbs fast without a greasy film</td></tr><tr><td>"Oil-free" / "non-comedogenic"</td><td>Won't clog pores</td></tr><tr><td>Hyaluronic acid, glycerin</td><td>Water-based hydration, not oil</td></tr><tr><td>Niacinamide</td><td>Bonus oil control and pore-refining</td></tr><tr><td>Lightweight lotion</td><td>Enough for combination skin without heaviness</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">What to avoid</h2>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Heavy, rich creams</strong> with lots of oils or butters — save those for dry winter skin.</li>
<li><strong>Anything that feels occlusive</strong> or leaves a film in the heat.</li>
<li><strong>Skipping it entirely</strong> — the worst option of all.</li>
</ul>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">How to use it</h2>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li>Apply to slightly damp skin after cleansing and serum — a little goes a long way.</li>
<li>In summer, a thin layer of gel moisturiser is plenty; layer up only in winter.</li>
<li>Always follow with sunscreen in the morning.</li>
</ul>
<p>Not sure where moisturiser fits? See our <a href="/blog/skincare-routine-order-pakistan">skincare routine order guide</a>.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Best moisturisers for oily skin in Pakistan</h2>
<p>All authentic, imported and available with cash on delivery nationwide:</p>
<ul class="wp-block-list">
<li><strong>Lightweight everyday lotion:</strong> the <a href="/product/cerave-moisturizing-lotion">CeraVe Daily Moisturizing Lotion</a> hydrates with ceramides and hyaluronic acid in a fast-absorbing, non-greasy formula.</li>
<li><strong>Refreshing gel-cream:</strong> the <a href="/product/medicube-collagen-jelly-cream">Medicube Collagen Jelly Cream</a> is a bouncy, water-light gel that sinks in instantly — ideal for humidity.</li>
<li><strong>Minimalist option:</strong> the <a href="/product/mixsoon-bean-cream">Mixsoon Bean Cream</a> is a clean, lightweight daily moisturiser.</li>
<li><strong>Oil control + hydration:</strong> the <a href="/product/medicube-txa-niacinamide-capsule-cream">Medicube TXA + Niacinamide Capsule Cream</a> adds tone-evening niacinamide.</li>
<li><strong>For drier days/winter:</strong> the richer <a href="/product/dr-althea-345-relief-cream">Dr.Althea 345 Relief Cream</a>.</li>
</ul>
<p>Browse all <a href="/shop?category=Moisturizers">moisturisers</a> or the full <a href="/shop?taxon=skincare">skincare</a> range.</p><a class="blog-cta" href="/product/medicube-collagen-jelly-cream">Shop the Medicube Collagen Jelly Cream →</a>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Should oily skin use moisturiser?</h3>
<p>Yes — always. Skipping it makes skin overproduce oil and weakens the barrier. Use a lightweight, oil-free gel or lotion.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Which moisturiser is best for oily skin in summer?</h3>
<p>A gel or gel-cream texture labelled oil-free/non-comedogenic. It hydrates without the greasy, heavy feel of a rich cream.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Is gel or cream better for oily skin?</h3>
<p>Gel, generally — it's water-light and absorbs fast. Save richer creams for dry skin or winter.</p>
<h3 class="wp-block-heading">Does moisturiser cause more oil or pimples?</h3>
<p>The right one doesn't. Choose non-comedogenic, oil-free formulas — the wrong heavy creams are what clog pores, not moisturiser itself.</p>
<h2 class="wp-block-heading">The bottom line</h2>
<p>Oily skin needs hydration just as much as any other type — it just needs it light. A gel or oil-free lotion keeps oil glands calm and the barrier strong. The <a href="/product/medicube-collagen-jelly-cream">Medicube Collagen Jelly Cream</a> and <a href="/product/cerave-moisturizing-lotion">CeraVe Daily Lotion</a> are two reliable picks — authentic, with cash on delivery across Pakistan.</p>$html$
